17:13:14Z"},"comments":6,"created_at":"2025-08-04T15:17:18Z","updated_at":"2025-08-13T08:31:00Z","closed_at":"2025-08-13T00:19:02Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.4\n\n### System information\n\nN/A\n\n### Issue description\n\nCan't compile on older Linux systems that the docs recommend me to compile on\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI'm building my own export templates for Godot 4.4. I don't have any issues on my system, but the [docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/contributing/development/compiling/compiling_for_linuxbsd.html#building-export-templates) say:\n\n> Linux binaries usually won't run on distributions that are older than the distribution they were built on. If you wish to distribute binaries that work on most distributions, you should build them on an old distribution such as Ubuntu 16.04. You can use a virtual machine or a container to set up a suitable build environment.\n\nSo I installed a VM with Ubuntu 16.04, but scons throws:\n\n```\nscons: Reading SConscript files ...\n  File \"/home/test/godot/SConstruct\", line 316\n\n    print(f\"Automatically detected platform: {env['platform']}\")\n```\n\n[It seems that](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/42126794/why-am-i-getting-invalid-syntax-from-an-f-string) the 'f\"text\"' syntax was only added in Python 3.6, and Ubuntu 16.04 comes with Python 2.7. \n\nI can [install Python 3.6](https://askubuntu.com/questions/865554/how-do-i-install-python-3-6-using-apt-get) and [make scons use it](https://stackoverflow.com/a/48212242), but it seems the newest version of scons available on Ubuntu 16.04 is 2.4.1-1, which:\n\n`scons: *** SCons version 2.4.1 does not run under Python version 3.6.10.`\n`scons is already the newest version (2.4.1-1).`\n\nSo where do I go from here? How do I compile a template on Linux without ruining compatibility for older systems, or I guess, how are the official Linux templates compiled?\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"skyace65","id":6080368,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwODAzNjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6080368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65","html_url":"https://github.com/skyace65","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109303/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109303/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}